# crafting_opened — the chip is the menu
#
# "At work: …" is followed, on the CONTINUE, by the crafting menu at that station for that trade, and
# what the menu does is real: the hammer's own iron is not touched, a horseshoe broken down gives two
# units of metal, and a nail made from them is in the pack afterwards.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm blacksmithing --grant-item hammer,horseshoe --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Ruin" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Old Anvil"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal use
means blacksmithing
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect At work:
expect-outcome crafting_opened
state
click button
wait mode Crafting 30
expect-state crafting trade=blacksmithing material=metal pool=0
expect-state crafting make item=nail cost=1 difficulty=1
expect-state crafting price=7 can=no
craft break horseshoe
expect-state crafting pool=2
expect-state crafting price=7 can=yes
craft make nail
craft settle
craft make nail
craft settle
expect-state crafting pool=0
craft leave
wait mode LocationInteraction 30
expect-state items nail
expect-state items hammer
expect-no-state items horseshoe
quit
